rson_id":"tvfy_10081","person_slug":"tony-burke","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Windsor","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10676","person_slug":"tony-windsor","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tony Zappia","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10695","person_slug":"tony-zappia","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Warren Snowdon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10599","person_slug":"warren-snowdon","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Wayne Swan","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10617","person_slug":"wayne-swan","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Wilson Tuckey","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10642","person_slug":"wilson-tuckey","vote":"no"},{"name":"Yvette D'Ath","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10164","person_slug":"yvette-dath","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Customs Tariff Amendment (2009 Measures No. 1) Bill 2009 [No. 2] - Second Reading - Read a second","noes":3,"question":"The majority voted in favour of a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org/debates/?id=2009-06-22.80.1) to read the bill for a second time.(Read more about the stages that a bill must pass through [here](http://www.peo.gov.au/learning/fact-sheets/making-a-law.html). ) This means that the majority agree with the main idea of the bill and that the House of Representatives can now discuss the bill in more detail. _Background to the bill_ The [bill](http://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/Bills_Search_Results/Result?bId=r4159) was introduced with the [Excise Tariff Amendment (2009 Measures No. 1) Bill 2009 (No. 2)](http://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/Bills_Search_Results/Result?bId=r4158) to increase the customs duty rate applying to certain alcoholic beverages ('alcopops') from $39.36 to $66.67 per litre of alcohol content and alters the taxation definitions of 'beer' and 'grape wine product'.(Read more about the bill in its [bills digest](http://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/bd/bd0809/09bd181).)","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-representatives-642","source_u